*.pem
# Two named exceptions to `*.pem`, both PUBLIC and both required for TLS
# verification to work at all. The blanket rule above still covers every other
# .pem in this repo, which is the point of naming these two rather than
# loosening it. Each file's own header block says what it is.
#   - the CA intermediate www.parkinginfo.ntpc.gov.tw does not send. A public
#     certificate, no key; without it New Taipei cannot build a chain and fails
#     every tick (docs/sources.md, "Known limits").
#   - a throwaway self-signed localhost cert AND KEY used by exactly one test,
#     which checks that Kaohsiung's and Hsinchu's relaxed context still refuses
#     an untrusted certificate. The key is deliberately public and worthless:
#     it is in no trust store, signs nothing but a loopback socket inside the
#     test suite, and is the same arrangement CPython's own ssl tests use.
!src/parkcast/sources/twca-ssl-ca-2023.pem
!tests/fixtures/selfsigned-localhost-keycert.pem
worker/node_modules/
web/.dev-artifacts/
